4.1.3 Robustness to threshold choices. Because the thresholds are
set by hand, we verified that the conversational-floor–dominance
relationships do not hinge on their exact values. Re-deriving the
competitive-interruption features over a grid of 36 settings (settling
time ∈{1.0,1.5,2.0,3.0}s, merge gap ∈{1.0,1.5,2.5}s, resolution
window ∈{4,6,8}s) leaves every feature’s sign unchanged and its
correlation with the averaged peer rating within a narrow band
across all cells (e.g., successful turn switch 𝜌 ∈[0.18,0.46], unre-
solved floor fight 𝜌 ∈[0.34,0.53]; the count of competitive attempts
is invariant by construction at 𝜌= 0.47). We fix the thresholds at
settling= 2.0 s, merge gap= 1.5 s, and window= 6.0 s.